WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:04.252
Legal teams work across agreements, amendments, correspondence, policies and
exhibits.

00:04.252 --> 00:13.226
Before advice is formed or a position is approved, the lawyer needs the
governing clause, the relevant version and a clear route back

00:13.226 --> 00:14.396
to the record.

00:14.396 --> 00:22.200
When the matter set is complex, experienced people spend time reconstructing
relationships that should be visible at the point of

00:22.200 --> 00:22.590
review.

00:23.590 --> 00:30.597
The apparent answer may sit in the main agreement, an amendment, a schedule,
later correspondence or an incorporated policy.

00:30.597 --> 00:32.442
A defined term can change.

00:32.442 --> 00:34.286
A clause can be replaced.

00:34.286 --> 00:37.605
A document can apply only from a particular date.

00:37.605 --> 00:40.187
The challenge is not simply retrieving text.

00:40.187 --> 00:45.350
It is identifying the relationships, chronology and authority that a human
reviewer must assess.

00:46.350 --> 00:52.661
The credible starting point is a closed, non-live matter set with permissions
already resolved.

00:52.661 --> 00:58.521
Agree the documents, factual questions, access boundary and evaluation
standard before testing begins.

00:58.521 --> 01:03.930
Include amendments, incomplete references, inconsistent terms and questions
the system should refuse.

01:03.930 --> 01:09.790
Compare matched tasks against the current process, with authorised reviewers
adjudicating every result.

01:10.790 --> 01:16.842
Cortessa is intended to operate on a dedicated sovereign workstation inside an
agreed boundary.

01:16.842 --> 01:22.893
The approved corpus, local index, on-device model and source viewer remain
within that environment.

01:22.893 --> 01:27.216
Runtime operation does not depend on a public cloud service.

01:27.216 --> 01:30.674
The organisation defines identity, permissions and security controls.

01:30.674 --> 01:37.590
Cortessa does not guarantee privilege or confidentiality, and it does not
widen access to the matter.

01:38.590 --> 01:41.584
Audit is the centre of the Cortessa workflow.

01:41.584 --> 01:50.191
Across the bounded matter set, it can surface an amendment that appears to
replace a clause, an exhibit that cites a missing source,

01:50.191 --> 01:53.559
inconsistent defined terms, uncertain dates or a broken reference.

01:53.559 --> 01:56.928
Each candidate enters legal review as a documentary question.

01:56.928 --> 02:00.670
It is not legal advice or a concluded legal finding.

02:01.670 --> 02:06.840
Each audit result leads back to the document and passage that created it.

02:06.840 --> 02:12.806
The lawyer can open the source, inspect the surrounding clause and assess
chronology and hierarchy.

02:12.806 --> 02:17.976
If the evidence is absent, Cortessa can refuse rather than fill the gap.

02:17.976 --> 02:25.135
The legal reviewer determines significance, accepts or rejects the candidate,
and records the outcome through the existing process.

02:25.135 --> 02:29.510
Verified shows provenance; it does not establish interpretation or legal
accuracy.

02:30.510 --> 02:37.321
Client instructions, legal context, professional duties and strategic
consequences cannot be delegated to a language model.

02:37.321 --> 02:40.726
Cortessa can expose the evidence route and uncertainty.

02:40.726 --> 02:46.685
A qualified lawyer decides what governs, what it means and what action is
appropriate.

02:46.685 --> 02:53.070
Cortessa does not replace a solicitor, form a legal position, decide privilege
or determine disclosure.

02:54.070 --> 03:00.509
Reviewers need the source route, document state and the policy governing what
the system may present.

03:00.509 --> 03:04.935
Identity, document currency, assertion policy and egress posture remain
visible concerns.

03:04.935 --> 03:12.582
Local activity can be recorded in a ledger so the organisation can inspect
what the system did and when.

03:12.582 --> 03:19.825
That record can support an evidence package, but it does not establish
accuracy, privilege, confidentiality or compliance with

03:19.825 --> 03:20.630
professional obligations.

03:21.630 --> 03:24.878
Compare matched tasks against the current workflow.

03:24.878 --> 03:31.838
Measure time to the relevant clause, citation completeness, amendment
visibility, correct refusals, reviewer effort and

03:31.838 --> 03:32.302
reproducibility.

03:32.302 --> 03:36.014
Include ambiguous drafting, missing documents and conflicting provisions.

03:36.014 --> 03:38.798
Record corpus preparation and setup effort.

03:38.798 --> 03:47.150
The result should show where Cortessa helps, where it fails and what must
change before any broader evaluation.

03:48.150 --> 03:54.853
Bring one closed, appropriately controlled matter set and the legal
professionals authorised to review it.

03:54.853 --> 03:58.876
Evaluate the evidence route, remediate observed gaps and retest.

03:58.876 --> 04:01.110
Start a conversation with Cortessa.
